{:edb/db-before-t 1998 :edb/db-after-t 1999 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535311 50 #inst "2026-10-08T21:48:47.571Z" 13194139535311 true] [17592186100868 1020 #edb/ref 17592186343182 13194139535311 true] [17592186100868 1020 #edb/ref 17592186343189 13194139535311 true] [17592186100868 1020 #edb/ref 17592186343196 13194139535311 true] [17592186343182 1017 #edb/ref 17592186343183 13194139535311 true] [17592186343182 1089 "q-141113" 13194139535311 true] [17592186343182 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535311 true] [17592186343182 1100 "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{2y}{x},\\,y(2)=-1.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=\\frac{A}{{x}^{2}}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$" 13194139535311 true] [17592186343182 1113 #uuid "0e0065e9-3a69-5f85-ad17-2869bffc442f" 13194139535311 true] [17592186343182 1145 "We're given that $y=\\frac{A}{{x}^{2}}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(2)=-1.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(2)=-1$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{A}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{A}{{2}^{2}} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{A}{4} \\\\ A & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$" 13194139535311 true] [17592186343183 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343184 13194139535311 true] [17592186343183 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343185 13194139535311 true] [17592186343183 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343186 13194139535311 true] [17592186343183 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343187 13194139535311 true] [17592186343183 1000 #edb/ref 17592186343188 13194139535311 true] [17592186343183 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535311 true] [17592186343183 1041 "selection" 13194139535311 true] [17592186343183 1104 #edb/ref 17592186343186 13194139535311 true] [17592186343183 1110 #uuid "ab99ede8-c73a-5acb-986d-4